          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Begin with the terrain. More than an acre of mostly level ground means a zero-turn will save you real time every week; hills, towing or plowing mean a tractor is the better buy. Next, size the deck to your gates and obstacles rather than acreage alone, and put your money into the transaxles and deck before horsepower.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            The Ariens IKON XD 52 and Husqvarna Z254F strike the best balance for most homeowners. Owners of large properties who want a mower for the long haul should look at the Toro TITAN MAX, and anyone ready to leave gas behind should price an EGO Z6 with enough batteries for their lawn.
